124 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 44 0 R
/T (5.1 Breadth-First Search \(BFS\) Uses a deque as a FIFO queue. Expands nodes layer by layer, guaranteeing the minimum number of steps to the goal on unweighted grids. A visited dictionary tracks seen positions to prevent re-expansion. BFS does not account for terrain costs, so it may not return the cheapest path on weighted maps. 5.2 Uniform Cost Search \(UCS\) Uses a min-heap \(heapq\) ordered by cumulative cost g\(n\). Always expands the cheapest frontier node, guaranteeing optimal cost on weighted graphs. UCS is equivalent to Dijkstra's algorithm and naturally handles variable terrain costs.)
/E (5.1 Breadth-First Search \(BFS\) Uses a deque as a FIFO queue. Expands nodes layer by layer, guaranteeing the minimum number of steps to the goal on unweighted grids. A visited dictionary tracks seen positions to prevent re-expansion. BFS does not account for terrain costs, so it may not return the cheapest path on weighted maps. 5.2 Uniform Cost Search \(UCS\) Uses a min-heap \(heapq\) ordered by cumulative cost g\(n\). Always expands the cheapest frontier node, guaranteeing optimal cost on weighted graphs. UCS is equivalent to Dijkstra's algorithm and naturally handles variable terrain costs.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [29]
>>
endobj
